//     keen-wren-419 STOP (T-4.6 formats, msg_0da56c18) foreclosed.
//     Defer-with-named-trigger, never stub.
//
//   - Python async / await semantics (`async def`, `.await`,
//     coroutines, async generators, async iterators): the COROUTINE
//     and ASYNC-ITERATION carriers compose over the type-system
//     declarations here (an `async def` returns a coroutine-typed
//     value), but the coordination-effect typing is owned by
//     extdeps/coordination.dag (T-4.8, IN-B effect-typed Bind
//     carriers — the same substrate that owns Rust's async / Verilog
//     concurrency / ptx SIMT-Bind effect typing); not authored here.
//
//   - Python exception flow (`raise` / `try / except / finally`):
//     RIDES the ratified `Outcome<T>` D1 carrier — Python's
//     exception is a structural error path on a typed return, and
//     the carrier is exactly the Outcome shape D1 ratifies. The
//     pipeline-stage operations (T-7 parse / T-10 emit) plug the
//     exception flow into Outcome when D1 lands; not authored here.
//
//   - Python duck-typing / structural-typing surface (protocols per
//     PEP 544, `typing.Protocol`). Python's nominal class hierarchy
//     is what `class X:` declares; structural typing through
//     protocols is RUNTIME structural-compatibility, modeled at the
//     LanguageModel grammar layer (T-4 bundled work) when type
//     annotations parse. The numeric-tower partition declared here
//     IS a structural sub-typing fact at the BUILT-IN-spec layer
//     (PEP 3141 ABC hierarchy is part of the language reference, not
//     a library protocol); user-defined protocols ride T-4 grammar.
//
//   - Python per-spec-operation cost INSTANCE-VALUES (concrete
//     `PythonCost { operation_cost: 1, allocation_cost: 0 }` rows per
//     spec-defined operation — the Reference §6 expressions / §8
//     statements partition; NOT per CPython-bytecode op, which is
//     CPython implementation detail per the `dis` module docs and
//     varies across versions / alternative VMs (PyPy / Jython /
//     GraalPython / MicroPython)): the carrier SHAPE is owned here
//     (PythonCost below); concrete cost rows ride T-12 lens/cost.dag
//     + U2 (the per-target projection of U1's `Homomorphism<…, …,
//     PythonScalar>.map`). Pre-T-12 instance-values would parallel-
//     represent the cost the map structurally encodes — the U1
//     no-engine smell (algebra.dag U1).
//
// Consumes (traceability / authority naming — STRUCTURE.md kernel-ambient
//   discipline: `Bool` / `Int` / `String` / `Char` / `List` / `Map` resolve
//   WITHOUT an import when used as type parameters / field types; the std/
//   file remains sole authority. Non-kernel std/ types used in alias-
//   identity MUST use explicit `import` when those rows land — not yet
//   for Int8..Float64 ladder (🟡 TRACKED-SCAFFOLD).):
//   - std/logic.dag: `Bool` — sole authority for the bivalent carrier
//     referenced by `type PyBool = Bool` (D2a(1)); merged 2026-05-16
